# Website design + copy rules

Applies to everything under `website/`. The site is pre-launch gated: keep
`noindex` meta and `robots.txt` until LAUNCH.md says otherwise.

## Stack (non-negotiable)

- Static HTML + CSS + vanilla JS only. **No frameworks, no build step, no
  webfonts, no external assets.** Speed is a product claim; the site must
  prove it. System font stack everywhere:
  `system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,"Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif`
- Icons: inline SVG only, geometric stroke style (1.8px stroke, round caps,
  `currentColor` or brand blue). **No emoji, no AI-sparkle/robot/wand
  iconography, no "AI" badges** — ever. No stock photos.
- CSP allows inline `<script>`/`style>` (`'unsafe-inline'`); `connect-src`
  permits only `api.shamarrconnect.com`. Keep all JS inline and small.

## Design tokens

Use the shared variables, don't invent new ones:
`--brand:#2B5CE6; --brand-dark:#1E3FA8; --brand-soft:#EAF0FF; --ink:#0F1B33;
--muted:#5A6B85; --line:#E6ECF5; --bg:#FFFFFF; --bg-soft:#F8FAFF; --ok:#16A34A;
--radius:16px; --shadow / --shadow-lg (blue-tinted).`
Dark sections use the navy gradient `linear-gradient(135deg,#0F1B33,#1E2F5C)`.
Headings: `letter-spacing:-.02/-.03em`, `text-wrap:balance`, weight 800.
Interactive elements get hover lift (`translateY(-1..-4px)` + shadow) and
`:focus-visible` outlines. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Brand

- Header brand is always `<img src="/wordmark.svg">` — never re-typeset
  "ShamarrConnect" as header text, never recolor it.
- Footer brand is plain text (no mark).
- Page titles: `Page · ShamarrConnect`; home: `ShamarrConnect: your computers, from anywhere`.

## Copy (plain-language rules)

- Write for a non-technical Nigerian business owner. No jargon ("end-to-end
  encrypted" → "locked end-to-end / scrambled data we cannot read"), no scary
  terms, no marketing-speak ("revolutionary", "seamless"), no exclamation marks.
- **Repeat the core promise through lenses** (the TeamViewer pattern): the same
  value — fast, private, run-for-you, monthly billing — restated per audience
  (personal / small business / IT support / schools & cybercafés) and per use
  case. Each section headline must stand alone in plain words.
- Currency/pricing mentions MUST use `<span data-region="ng">` /
  `data-region="intl"` variants — the edge middleware strips the non-matching
  one. Never hardcode one currency.
- Competitor comparisons: structural facts only (billing cadence, free tier,
  open source), date-stamped, no exact competitor prices. No superlatives we
  can't defend.
- Industry/audience sections: describe the industry's problem + our real
  capabilities (reach, support, watch over machines) only. Never claim
  certifications (HIPAA/PCI/ISO), government approval, or existing customers.
  No "trusted by" until it is literally true.

## Structure

- Every page: sticky header (wordmark + nav + CTA), content sections
  alternating white / `--bg-soft` / navy band, footer (plain-text brand,
  Product/Resources/Company columns).
- The waitlist form posts to `/api/waitlist` (honeypot field `company`);
  keep it working and CSP-safe.
- New pages need: noindex meta, description meta (region variants if it
  mentions price/currency), favicon links, wordmark header, footer.
